---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { content } from '../data/content';

const t = content.en;
const github = 'https://github.com/hackills/munadi-apks';
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy — GitHub build — Munadi"
  description="How the GitHub build of Munadi handles data: no accounts, ads, analytics, or trackers. Approximate location is used only for Qibla, the place name, and the prayer-time area."
>
  <Header lang="en" t={t} home="/" alternatePath="/ar/" />

  <main id="main">
    <section class="document-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p>
          This policy covers the <strong>GitHub build</strong> of Munadi, the signed APK
          downloaded from GitHub Releases. That build can check GitHub for updates and
          install them itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container">
      <article class="document">
        <p class="effective">Effective: 4 November 2026</p>

        <p class="note">
          <strong>Installed from Google Play?</strong> The Play build has no internet
          permission and no in-app updater, so it has its own policy:
          <a href="/privacy/play/">read the Google Play build policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No accounts, ads, analytics, or trackers.</li>
          <li>Prayer times and settings stay on your device.</li>
          <li>
            Approximate location is used for the Qibla compass, the place name, and the
            prayer-time area.
          </li>
          <li>We do not operate a server that receives your data.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Data the app uses</h2>

        <h3>Approximate location</h3>
        <p>
          Munadi requests <strong>approximate location only</strong>; precise location
          is not requested. It is used to calculate the Qibla direction and distance,
          show a place name, and suggest the nearest prayer-time area. The last
          approximate location and place are cached in the app’s private storage so the
          Qibla screen can open quickly.
        </p>
        <p>
          Place names are matched on the device from a built-in list. When location is
          already allowed, the app may check it at launch to suggest an area. Your
          location is not sent anywhere.
        </p>

        <h3>Settings and timetable</h3>
        <p>
          Theme, color, language, prayer-time area, iqamah adjustments, notification
          preferences, and sound choices are stored locally on your device. The Qatar
          Calendar House timetable is built into the APK.
        </p>
        <p>
          Prayer times use the Doha table by default. You can choose Abu Samra, Dukhan,
          or Al Shamal in Settings, and the app may suggest one when location is
          available.
        </p>

        <h3>Network access</h3>
        <p>
          If update checks are enabled, the app requests the latest release information
          from GitHub. GitHub receives standard network information such as your IP
          address and the app’s user agent, subject to GitHub’s privacy policy. Munadi
          does not send analytics, identifiers, or usage data.
        </p>

        <h3>Permissions</h3>
        <p>Depending on the features you use, the app may request:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Approximate location, for Qibla and the prayer-time area</li>
          <li>Notifications, for adhan, iqamah, and update alerts</li>
          <li>Exact alarms, to keep prayer reminders on time</li>
          <li>Battery optimisation exemption, so alarms are not delayed</li>
          <li>Internet, for optional update checks</li>
          <li>Install unknown apps, for in-app updates</li>
          <li>Foreground media playback and vibration, for the adhan</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can decline optional permissions and still use the prayer timetable.</p>

        <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell or share your data. Munadi has no accounts and no analytics
          SDK. Local data remains until you clear the app’s storage or uninstall it.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Munadi is a general-audience prayer app and does not knowingly collect
          personal information from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated in the public repository. The effective date above
          will change when it does.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:munadi.prayer@gmail.com">munadi.prayer@gmail.com</a>,
          or open an issue at
          <a href={`${github}/issues`} rel="noopener">{github}/issues</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="note">
          <h3>This website</h3>
          <p>
            This site is a static page hosted on Vercel. It uses no cookies, analytics,
            or tracking scripts. Vercel processes standard request information — such
            as your IP address and user agent — to serve and protect the site, subject
            to Vercel’s privacy policy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer lang="en" t={t} home="/" />
</Base>
